📄 XML files ka matlab kya hota hai?
🔴 Old Spring (without Spring Boot)

Pehle Spring applications me beans aur server XML files me define karne padte the.

Example: applicationContext.xml
<beans>
    <bean id="userService" class="com.example.UserService"/>

    <bean id="userRepository" class="com.example.UserRepository"/>

    <bean id="dataSource"
          class="org.apache.commons.dbcp.BasicDataSource">
        <property name="url" value="jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/db"/>
        <property name="username" value="root"/>
        <property name="password" value="root"/>
    </bean>
</beans>


😵 Bohat zyada:

Boilerplate

Error-prone

Hard to maintain

⚙️ Manual server setup (old days)
web.xml
<web-app>
    <servlet>
        <servlet-name>dispatcher</servlet-name>
        <servlet-class>
            org.springframework.web.servlet.DispatcherServlet
        </servlet-class>
    </servlet>

    <servlet-mapping>
        <servlet-name>dispatcher</servlet-name>
        <url-pattern>/</url-pattern>
    </servlet-mapping>
</web-app>


Har cheez manually 😓

🚀 Spring Boot me kya hota hai?
✅ No XML required
@SpringBootApplication
public class App {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SpringApplication.run(App.class, args);
    }
}

Beans:
@Service
public class UserService { }

DB config:
spring.datasource.url=jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/db
spring.datasource.username=root
spring.datasource.password=root

🧠 Auto-configuration ka matlab

Spring Boot:

Starter dependency dekhta hai (spring-boot-starter-data-jpa)

Automatically:

DataSource banata hai

EntityManager configure karta hai

Transaction manager set karta hai

Embedded Tomcat start karta hai

🏁 One-liner (interview ready)

“XML files refer to old Spring configuration files like applicationContext.xml and web.xml, which Spring Boot replaces with annotations and auto-configuration.”

⚠️ Important clarification

Spring Boot:

❌ XML for configuration avoid karta hai

✅ XML for other purposes ho sakti hain (Hibernate mapping, legacy integration)